      "impact": "This shorts an Ethernet differential transmit pair to ground and may prevent that port from operating or stress the module’s PHY.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U1", "U3"],
      "pins": ["U1.5", "U1.6", "U1.7", "U1.8", "U1.9", "U3.7", "U3.9", "U3.10", "U3.17", "U3.19"],
      "nets": ["NET0022", "NET0020", "NET0007", "NET0049", "NET0048"],
      "observed": "The keyboard’s five column outputs share nets with SKW92A pins identified as Ethernet signals: COL1–COL5 connect respectively to LAN_PORT1_TX+, LAN_PORT1_TX-, LAN_PORT1_RX+, LAN_PORT1_RX-, and LAN_PORT2_RX+.",
      "expected": "As the specification states, the keyboard matrix lines should connect to GPIOs, not be electrically shared with Ethernet port signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0022\") (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX+\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"COL1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0020\") (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_TX-\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"COL2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"NET0007\") (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT1_RX+\")) (node (ref \"U3\") (pin \"10\") (pinfunction \"COL3\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "netlist shows 5 column + 7 row lines wired directly to SKW92A GPIO pins"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Scanning the keyboard can drive or load Ethernet PHY signals, while Ethernet activity can interfere with keyboard scanning; the affected Ethernet functions may also be unusable.",
      "confidence": 0.93
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows a SKW92A Ethernet transmit pair hard-shorted to ground and keyboard columns sharing nets with Ethernet signals. Both are direct connectivity conflicts with the stated design and are likely to impair module interfaces."
}

